<title>USA: Telefonica del Peru sees 1997 revenues cut.</title>
<headline>Telefonica del Peru sees 1997 revenues cut.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telefonica del Peru said a recently-announced 35 percent reduction of rental line and data transmission circuit tariffs will result in more than 17 million soles of lower 1997 revenue for the company.</p>
<p>The company said the tariff reduction by OSIPTEL (Organization for the Supervision of Private Investment in Telecommunications) is &quot;not justified.&quot;  The company added that it would try to resolve the matter according to the legal procedures outlined in its Concession Agreement with OSIPTEL.</p>
<p>The tariffs had been fixed since June 1993, the company said.</p>
</text>
